## Outcome and scope

Read physical [0x00000000,0x00020000) twice through /dev/mem. Both complete
131072-byte acquisitions are byte-identical, SHA256:
  c1a7d8ffc9a3b9581953107861e61d9d7d9b9b2c5dafd929571446614884f92e

Coherent reset/startup code, PBL source identifiers, authentication/flash/USB
code, ROM version strings, and fixed low-address references identify the
captured contents convincingly as Qualcomm PBL. The layout agrees with the
related-chip ROM mapping. Repeat reads alone do not prove silicon mask-ROM
backing, rule out a mirror/alias, or establish that every ROM on the SoC was
captured. No unsigned-loader execution or secure-boot bypass was attempted.
The repeats are from one diagnostic boot, not independent cold-boot captures.

No EDL programmer or TrustZone exploit was used. The reader makes aligned
volatile 32-bit reads through an O_RDONLY|O_SYNC, PROT_READ|MAP_SHARED mapping.
No flash-writing commands, physical-memory writes, or manual security-register
writes were issued. The full persistent BOOT partition remained identical.
The device was returned to its original Pocketboot kernel with ADB/fastboot
working; /dev/mem is absent again.

