The code is consistent with the RPM ARM7 primary-boot role documented for
APQ8064. This corroborates related-chip documentation; it does not independently
identify the executing core or validate the original generic boot-chain diagram.

## Transport incident and restored device

After successful acquisition and a successful post-read dmesg retrieval, an
inline final-inventory command exceeded fastboot's64-byte command buffer:
  oem shell:uname -a; cat /proc/uptime /sys/devices/soc0/soc_id /sys/devices/system/cpu/online
This request is92 bytes. It timed out, and a subsequent short getvar product
also timed out. ADB still executed uname and dmesg; kernel remained7.1.0-rc3-pbl.
No explicit transport-error/overflow log was found in the captured dmesg.
The overlong request is the observed trigger, not a diagnosed kernel fault.
Longer scripts must use stage + oem shell-staged; documented read commands are
29..35 bytes including the oem prefix. USB robustness is a separate follow-up.

Before reboot, retrieved the full persistent BOOT through ADB and compared it:
  adb -s 00001EB100006FAB exec-out 'cat /dev/mmcblk0p7' > boot-after.img
  cmp target/pbl-lab/boot-before.img boot-after.img
